The above covers this package's own source. It does not cover the compiled
artifact it ships: `rbcop_fmt.wasm.br` embeds rbcop, RuboCop's configuration and
that of seven RuboCop plugins (MIT), and the Rust crates it links - MIT where a
crate offers it, otherwise BSD-2-Clause, Unicode-3.0 or BSL-1.0 - and statically
links wasi-libc (MIT, with BSD parts).

Every one of those is permissive and asks at most for attribution. The notices
and the full texts are in `licenses/NOTICE.md`.
